# style: a comment block (`# name -- summary`, `usage:`, `args:`, `result:`, `errors:`) right
# before a stub `proc`, `constructor` or `method` with the real parameter list. The stubs sit
# inside `if {0} {...}`, so Tcl never runs them and the native commands stay in place.
#
# Conventions: objects are TclOO objects (`set obj [datamunge::Class new ...]`, `$obj method ...`,
# `$obj destroy`); every object a command returns is a new Tcl command that lives until it is
# destroyed (a borrowed one only drops the Tcl side). Lists are Tcl lists, maps dicts, pairs and
